From 307ab56d4ba9c1ce55592600081e4794e5642fab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@example.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:11:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 532/533] perf(sessions): page multi-segment lineage reads in
 SQL on display_identity

get_messages(include_ancestors=True) on a compression lineage read every row of
every segment and deduped/paged in Python, so a 200-row Desktop tail of a long
lineage shipped the whole transcript through Python first. Indexed segments now
group on the stored display_identity (the same sha256 of _display_dedupe_key the
Python fold uses) and page in SQL; rewind reads and read-only stores that cannot
backfill identities keep the Python fold, which is also the test oracle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
